From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 09:49:40 -0400
Subject: menus: Google's rows off the page and app menus, Import, Screenshot
 and Spaces in the app menu, menus per row kind, and wave 2's small rows

The page menu hides Lens, the Gemini rows, the QR code and reading mode
while the short-menus setting is on; the default engine's own search row
stays (docs/features/menus.md M2). The app menu hides Manage Google
account, Open Glic, Send tab to self, Customize Chrome, Payment methods,
the tab-groups and reading-list submenus and the bookmarks-bar and
side-panel rows, and gains Import, a Screenshot submenu with the three
captures and a Spaces submenu mirroring the menu bar's (M3). The tab menu
shows the rows that apply to the row's kind -- the essentials card keeps
neither pin nor folder nor Space rows, the Space-pinned row offers Unpin
and the home rows, the plain row neither -- through a visibility question
the collection controller answers with stedding::IsTabMenuCommandVisible;
a split row arranges its panes instead of offering a split; the folder
header gains a menu: Rename, Collapse or Expand, Move Tabs Out, Close the
folder's tabs (M7). "Move to Space" lists the window's other Spaces after
Rename, the selection moves and the window follows (M1).

The sidebar's own background menu loses Bookmark All Tabs, the Tab Search
and Glic pins and the auto-expanding toggle under the same setting; the
short tab menu carries extension rows again (Chromium's ExtensionItems test
is green). Also the small rows of wave 2: a folder dims once every tab
inside sleeps (tabs R7); a pin's hover card carries "Pinned in <Space> -
home <host>" (pins H8); a drifted essentials card shows a reset control in
its corner while the pointer rests on it (H10); the last pin's close has its
test (H11); the bar's tab rows step aside while a peek is open (commandbar
K16).

Why: docs/ROUND6-PLAN.md wave 2 (R6-14, and the small rows of R6-15, R6-16,
R6-11), Arc's menus: the browser's own verbs first, and nothing that
reaches Google by default.
Removable when: Chromium's menus can be curated without a fork.
